WEBVTT

00:08.220 --> 00:13.890
An aspiring serenade of instincts!

00:08.220 --> 00:13.890
Seijakusa wo ima uchikowasu yaketsuku honnou no sere naade

00:14.180 --> 00:19.400
Just once is alright, I want to tell you about the blooming impact!

00:14.180 --> 00:19.400
Ichido de iikara tsutaetai saki tagaru shou geki wo

00:21.480 --> 00:24.880
Yeah! Light Now, Scream now! Break the breaks!

00:21.480 --> 00:24.880
YEAH! Light now scream now bukkowase bureeki wa

00:25.190 --> 00:26.500
Wind speed is freedom, get on!

00:25.190 --> 00:26.500
fuusoku wa freedom norikomi na

00:26.510 --> 00:28.030
Mind style is E.G.O!

00:26.510 --> 00:28.030
mind style wa E.G.O

00:28.030 --> 00:30.540
Hiding the city's passing whispers

00:28.030 --> 00:30.540
Ikizuki machi koe wo hisome

00:30.620 --> 00:33.580
Seeking my presence.

00:30.620 --> 00:33.580
boku no sonzai wo motomeru

00:34.000 --> 00:36.620
The hings you want to protect...

00:34.000 --> 00:36.620
Mamoritai mono wa itsudatte

00:36.710 --> 00:39.580
Can never be protected.

00:36.710 --> 00:39.580
mamorenai koto wa bakari darou

00:39.590 --> 00:46.630
I know how much I'm worth cannot be changed but there's no reason to be swayed.

00:39.590 --> 00:46.630
Sadamerareta kachikan ni boku wo furuwasu imi nado nai yo

00:47.680 --> 00:53.360
I don't mind if I get hurt because you gave me a miracle.

00:47.680 --> 00:53.360
Kizutsuitemo katawanai kiseki wo kimi ga kureta kara

00:53.680 --> 00:58.140
Just once is alright, I want to tell you, we're winders!

00:53.680 --> 00:58.140
ichido de iikara tsutaetai, bokutachi ga WINDER

00:58.400 --> 01:01.380
If you choose to silently struggle against who you are

00:58.400 --> 01:01.380
Arisou de nai jibun rashisa ni

01:01.380 --> 01:04.280
that seems to be there but is not.

01:01.380 --> 01:04.280
koe mo dasezu mogakuno nara

01:04.280 --> 01:07.260
You probably should go to the self centered tomorrow I told you about

01:04.280 --> 01:07.260
Shi no go no iu, katte na ashita ni

01:07.300 --> 01:09.470
And...

01:07.300 --> 01:09.470
sakasete mita yo

01:09.530 --> 01:13.330
...The reality in your heart.

01:09.530 --> 01:13.330
kokoro no riaru

01:15.750 --> 01:19.370
I am right here.

01:15.750 --> 01:19.370
boku wa kokoni iru

01:22.770 --> 01:25.430
I want to flip light and darkness around, victorious return of the world.

01:22.770 --> 01:25.430
Hikari to kage tokkae WORLD he gaisen

01:25.630 --> 01:28.720
Now, the will to go towards the future and play on!

01:25.630 --> 01:28.720
Saa WILL TO GO mirai he to PLAY ON!

02:01.160 --> 02:01.950
All right!

02:35.070 --> 02:37.900
Mikoto's late getting up. That's pretty rare.

02:42.280 --> 02:43.240
I'll go call him.

02:46.790 --> 02:47.700
Onii-chan?

02:49.250 --> 02:52.250
I've gone to school. Please don't look for me.

02:54.330 --> 02:58.250
Mom! Onii-chan's already gone to school!

02:58.630 --> 03:00.760
So, he didn't oversleep after all.

03:26.410 --> 03:28.530
I'm currently riding right now.

03:29.620 --> 03:32.330
They were quick to give up.

03:33.170 --> 03:35.880
Then, let's go to the next problem, on the next page.

03:36.380 --> 03:38.790
The quadratic x...

03:42.510 --> 03:47.220
As I'm super late,

03:59.820 --> 04:00.940
Fukazawa-san...

04:02.900 --> 04:05.320
Why are you wearing a bathing suit?

04:05.490 --> 04:06.740
This way, I...

04:10.790 --> 04:13.040
Fu-Fukazawa-san.

04:14.750 --> 04:17.420
Huh? When did you put on your uniform?

04:19.340 --> 04:20.840
Where is this place?

04:22.590 --> 04:25.010
Oh, yeah. I was practicing all night,

04:25.550 --> 04:27.840
and fell asleep here.

04:40.770 --> 04:41.860
So, how was it?

04:42.320 --> 04:42.780
Yes?

04:43.690 --> 04:45.110
Didn't you practice?

04:45.740 --> 04:47.910
You can ride a bit now, right?

04:48.450 --> 04:53.240
Ah, no... That...

04:54.160 --> 04:56.660
But it's only been a day.

04:57.500 --> 04:57.960
But...

05:00.170 --> 05:04.260
But... That...

05:04.970 --> 05:09.840
after slowly practicing a bit, I was able to ride this far.

05:12.850 --> 05:17.690
Although It's only a little bit,

05:20.190 --> 05:21.110
Here, give me your hand.

05:24.440 --> 05:29.820
Really, who in the world would practice riding a bicycle to this extent?

05:31.120 --> 05:33.990
As I expected, Shinozaki is a bit weird.

05:35.500 --> 05:38.460
Fukazawa-san's hand... Is so warm.

05:41.290 --> 05:43.540
It'd be nice if I could transfer this feeling to her.

05:44.670 --> 05:45.550
All right. All done.

05:53.890 --> 05:55.680
I won't shower for the time being.

05:58.940 --> 06:02.150
Could you be skipping class today?

06:03.110 --> 06:07.820
Originally it really was...

06:09.240 --> 06:13.410
But Fukazawa-san said I'm a person with a strong heart.

06:14.330 --> 06:18.290
I wand to do my best to become that person you spoke of.

06:32.720 --> 06:35.970
Anyway, why is your underwear showing?

06:36.350 --> 06:41.270
No-No... Doesn't someone as fashionable as Fukazawa-san know?

06:41.900 --> 06:45.900
It's popular for young people these days to purposely show their underwear for others to see.

06:46.070 --> 06:50.150
No way. Who wants to show their underwear?

06:55.450 --> 06:56.530
That is definitely shown on purpose.

06:56.580 --> 06:57.370
Don't stare.

06:57.580 --> 06:58.740
Unbelievable.

07:04.290 --> 07:06.590
S-So, it was like that.

07:07.130 --> 07:08.630
Without a doubt.

07:09.630 --> 07:11.550
Then, what should I wear?

07:12.430 --> 07:16.550
Ahh! What is this?

07:16.970 --> 07:21.640
Blackout! Doomsday! Not good! Danger!

07:23.520 --> 07:23.810
Huh?

07:24.350 --> 07:28.440
This is for you.

07:29.320 --> 07:31.150
It's better than wearing nothing.

07:32.030 --> 07:33.240
Besides, that's just a cheap product.

07:34.410 --> 07:36.280
Just see it as a reward for your hard work.

07:37.200 --> 07:39.120
A-Are you really sincere?

07:41.200 --> 07:45.080
At this time you're supposed to say, "Are you really giving this to me?"

07:46.540 --> 07:47.840
Y-You're welcome.

07:49.130 --> 07:50.670
That's my line.

07:51.380 --> 07:54.970
All right. All right!

07:55.550 --> 07:57.510
Oh, yeah, Shinozaki.

08:02.770 --> 08:05.100
I'll tell you something really important.

08:07.440 --> 08:08.360
W-What is it?

08:09.110 --> 08:10.320
Lift it up a bit.

08:10.440 --> 08:11.190
Okay.

08:14.400 --> 08:16.070
The only thing wrong with people who don't know how to ride a bicycle,

08:16.570 --> 08:18.530
‌‌‌‌is that their balance isn't very good.

08:20.540 --> 08:22.290
Balance... Eh?

08:23.290 --> 08:29.500
Yep. They only think about stepping on the pedals, but don't consider how to not let the bicycle fall.

08:34.220 --> 08:36.340
So, adjust the gears,

08:36.550 --> 08:38.220
so that you can't push the pedals.

08:38.930 --> 08:41.310
Like this, you can't step on the pedals anymore.

08:42.140 --> 08:43.640
Who... Who knows...

08:44.770 --> 08:46.140
You're really pissing me off.

08:46.810 --> 08:50.230
All right. Just use this condition to practice your balance.

08:50.900 --> 08:52.190
Un-Understood!

09:11.090 --> 09:12.210
Use your legs more!

09:12.800 --> 09:14.710
Okay!

09:18.260 --> 09:20.720
Then, work hard!

09:21.850 --> 09:24.890
Fukazawa-san stalking off is pretty cute, too.

09:25.560 --> 09:30.190
Oh. This isn't the time to be fascinated.

09:31.230 --> 09:33.610
Balance. It's balance.

09:45.330 --> 09:52.750
What is this? I've already grasped the the sense of balance and moved 50 centimeters forward!

09:53.380 --> 09:56.130
Somehow I feel like I can see the light of hope!

10:06.140 --> 10:09.350
Sorry. My leg unconsciously extended itself out.

10:11.020 --> 10:13.440
You okay, boy?

10:16.110 --> 10:17.360
I-Izawa-san.

10:21.990 --> 10:24.490
What if you were sent to the guidance office?

10:24.950 --> 10:28.410
That's true.

10:28.830 --> 10:33.790
It's because we said we're going to karaoke.

10:34.040 --> 10:35.880
Is the school really a place to meet up?

10:36.300 --> 10:37.000
A middle stop.

10:48.560 --> 10:50.310
Umm... What is it?

10:50.980 --> 10:53.850
Where's lunch? It's already noon.

10:54.150 --> 10:58.030
S-Sorry. I forgot.

10:58.360 --> 11:00.820
Then take out your wallet and go buy them now.

11:01.780 --> 11:02.860
Steak!

11:03.320 --> 11:04.110
Fried rice.

11:04.280 --> 11:05.910
Raw beef. Goose liver sauce.

11:08.290 --> 11:13.080
I say, Shinozaki-san, didn't you ever think about changing yourself a little bit?

11:17.710 --> 11:18.250
What?

11:22.760 --> 11:25.300
No. Nothing.

11:26.350 --> 11:29.010
I'll buy them right away.

11:32.940 --> 11:35.270
Sorry, Fukazawa-san.

11:37.690 --> 11:40.570
What is this?

11:40.610 --> 11:41.650
You can't touch this!

11:50.450 --> 11:54.870
No... I didn't at that time...

11:55.210 --> 11:57.250
What am I doing?

11:58.590 --> 11:59.750
That's right. Hurry and apologize.

12:00.380 --> 12:02.970
If I quickly buy their lunch now, I can get their forgiveness.

12:04.470 --> 12:05.800
S-Sorry.

12:06.300 --> 12:08.220
Yes. Just like this.

12:08.720 --> 12:12.640
But, umm... I ask that you each get your own lunch.

12:13.350 --> 12:14.690
Huh?

12:15.560 --> 12:17.690
I won't obey your orders anymore.

12:18.650 --> 12:19.480
What are you talking about?

12:20.150 --> 12:21.820
I won't allow you to touch this.

12:21.990 --> 12:24.740
Hurry and shut up! You're asking to get beaten up.

12:25.660 --> 12:31.700
I... I learned this from a person I deeply admire.

12:32.040 --> 12:33.620
Ah, I get it, I get it.

12:33.710 --> 12:37.370
Just like in dramas, a type of role that fights back at the moment when he's about to lose.

12:38.210 --> 12:40.000
You're that type of person.

12:43.300 --> 12:47.800
Then, I am... The evil king in this plot.

12:52.560 --> 12:55.060
You... What do you understand?

12:58.440 --> 13:02.610
Even though it may seem like trash to you guys,

13:10.950 --> 13:13.740
You can't bring this to school.

13:14.000 --> 13:16.000
Too bad. Confiscated.

13:18.370 --> 13:19.630
So obedient.

13:29.590 --> 13:32.890
It hurts. What part of the arteries did he break?

13:34.020 --> 13:37.810
Speaking of which, I've never been beaten like this before.

13:39.350 --> 13:41.610
Because I always run away before getting beat up.

13:41.980 --> 13:44.860
But whatever.

13:45.280 --> 13:47.190
It would've been better to have immediately handed that thing over.

13:48.360 --> 13:50.410
That's right, eh.

13:51.240 --> 13:54.540
Just sitting like that, you'll never suffer again.

13:56.540 --> 14:00.250
If it was the me from yesterday, I think I'd probably do that.

14:02.340 --> 14:04.500
But... I'm not like that anymore.

14:10.470 --> 14:12.220
I... Will change the me from yesterday.

14:15.850 --> 14:18.020
What is that?

14:20.980 --> 14:22.810
So noisy.

14:24.610 --> 14:26.400
That was...

14:36.330 --> 14:38.370
Damn it. Damn it!

14:55.050 --> 14:59.560
Damn it. Move. Move! Move!!

15:24.670 --> 15:29.550
I don't know what's going on,

15:34.260 --> 15:35.050
Sit still.

15:37.220 --> 15:41.100
Head up, chest out.

15:44.900 --> 15:48.400
Even if the bicycle is wobbling, the body must remain perpendicular to the ground.

15:51.280 --> 15:53.320
The rest is believing in yourself.

15:57.990 --> 16:02.830
In the beginning, it was only a simple, unimpressive form of transportation,

16:04.210 --> 16:11.000
but after going through a 200 year long period of evolution,

16:11.710 --> 16:14.970
it has already come quite close to the top of its domain.

16:15.550 --> 16:18.550
Plus, progressing further now will return the power

16:19.260 --> 16:21.850
‌‌‌‌to its original power in the human body.

16:22.930 --> 16:24.600
If you so wish,

16:25.400 --> 16:28.650
‌‌if you can answer that voice,

16:29.770 --> 16:35.990
then you can call upon the great possibility sleeping within humans.

16:37.030 --> 16:39.910
So slow.

17:42.010 --> 17:43.100
I-Izawa-san!

17:45.810 --> 17:48.520
What is this sound?

17:49.270 --> 17:50.270
I've never heard this sound before.

17:51.400 --> 17:53.440
Could it be that my eardrums popped?

17:59.360 --> 18:01.160
No. It's my chest.

18:02.580 --> 18:07.540
What? This is the sound of my heart.

18:08.830 --> 18:12.080
It's a weird sound.

18:12.590 --> 18:14.210
It's obviously my chest that's beating, but the sound is resounding in my head.

18:16.840 --> 18:21.840
I feel kind of nauseous.

18:23.180 --> 18:26.810
But... occasionally being like this isn't too bad.

18:27.770 --> 18:29.390
After all, I'm still alive.

18:32.360 --> 18:34.110
In the end, the one chasing after them

18:34.320 --> 18:36.020
ended up with the severest wounds.

18:36.650 --> 18:37.530
Fukazawa-san.

18:38.690 --> 18:41.240
There are ones better than that.

18:42.030 --> 18:43.740
You're really a first-rate idiot.

18:53.210 --> 18:59.510
This one is seven billion times better than the others.

19:02.640 --> 19:08.010
Can't you think of a way to control that unreasonable enthusiasm?

19:08.770 --> 19:11.180
I really hope you won't pull me into it.

19:14.480 --> 19:15.860
W-What?

19:15.900 --> 19:16.690
I can ride it.

19:19.400 --> 19:23.950
Just now, I really rode this bicycle.

19:24.570 --> 19:25.570
Did you realize that now?

19:27.290 --> 19:30.620
Amazing.

19:31.040 --> 19:33.120
I, who couldn't do anything at first, actually could have such an awesome experience.

19:34.000 --> 19:38.500
Although my heart is still in a excited state and both my legs still hurt,

19:39.420 --> 19:42.800
but, because I was able to ride the bicycle, I was able to get the headband back.

19:43.840 --> 19:45.430
Bicycles are amazing.

19:45.930 --> 19:47.600
It's actually not that amazing.

19:48.430 --> 19:50.220
Bicycles aren't machines,

19:50.890 --> 19:52.640
‌and don't rely on gasoline to run.

19:53.940 --> 19:57.360
So, they aren't like some divine power.

19:57.730 --> 20:00.530
All of this is because of your own strength.

20:03.030 --> 20:05.450
All from my own strength?

20:07.910 --> 20:10.160
Bicycles are actually pretty interesting.

20:23.720 --> 20:25.760
These two days have been really nice.

20:26.840 --> 20:29.390
They were the happiest two days of my life so far.

20:30.930 --> 20:32.270
Is it okay to end it like this?

20:37.480 --> 20:42.150
Umm...

20:43.110 --> 20:43.940
I want to join the Bicycle Club.

20:44.820 --> 20:47.820
I want to bet my all on this bicycle.

20:49.830 --> 20:55.460
And... One day when I can rely upon this bicycle to take down the world,

20:56.170 --> 20:58.380
I hope Fukazawa-san will ride together with me.

21:01.960 --> 21:02.550
Together?

21:03.420 --> 21:06.800
Yes! Umm... Just a short distance apart.

21:07.340 --> 21:12.680
Fifty meters... Five meters...

21:13.220 --> 21:14.270
Is the "taking down the world"

21:14.310 --> 21:15.600
‌about becoming number one in the world?

21:16.140 --> 21:17.310
Y-Yes.

21:18.150 --> 21:21.900
Saying things like this might make Fukazawa-san think I like her.

21:22.780 --> 21:24.030
That's fine.

21:24.650 --> 21:25.940
R-Really?

21:26.570 --> 21:28.030
A-All right.

21:28.450 --> 21:29.200
But when the time comes,

21:29.370 --> 21:30.660
‌‌you'll be the one riding.

21:30.910 --> 21:33.660
T-That...

21:37.540 --> 21:40.380
If it's okay, please wear a bathing suit.

21:44.380 --> 21:48.930
Is this how it feels to talk to an idol on TV?

21:50.800 --> 21:54.140
That's just a simple desire... An ideal.

21:55.520 --> 21:57.560
It's a far away existence.

21:58.440 --> 21:59.940
But for now...

22:01.650 --> 22:04.570
That day, I had a person I liked.

22:08.900 --> 22:13.190
Kaze ga toorisugiteku

22:09.400 --> 22:13.690
The wind glides by,

22:14.280 --> 22:18.200
Karada wo surinukete

22:14.280 --> 22:18.200
Brushing against our body.

22:18.530 --> 22:23.990
Itsushika iro ase bokete shimatta

22:18.530 --> 22:23.990
The colors faded in the farthest end of the sky,

22:24.040 --> 22:28.120
Sora no saihate de

22:24.040 --> 22:28.120
before we realized.

22:29.170 --> 22:37.170
Nama atatakai kaze ga fuiteru fuiteru

22:29.170 --> 22:37.170
The luke warm breeze is blowing, blowing.

22:38.800 --> 22:42.600
Mujun darake no sekai de

22:38.800 --> 22:42.600
In a world full on inconsistency,

22:42.720 --> 22:48.430
Toke sou no kimi ga futto boku ni waraikaketa

22:42.720 --> 22:48.430
Melting into it, you grin at me with a whiff.

22:57.360 --> 23:01.950
Kaze ga toorisugiteku

22:57.360 --> 23:01.950
The wind glides by,

23:02.200 --> 23:05.830
Karada wo surinukete

23:02.200 --> 23:05.830
Brushing against our body.

23:06.410 --> 23:11.920
Itsushika a iro ase bokete shimatta

23:06.410 --> 23:11.920
The colors faded before we realized.

23:12.000 --> 23:21.130
Sora no saihate de aou

23:12.000 --> 23:21.130
Let's meet at the furthest end of the sky.
